{"Async function deleteScheduledEmailReminder is called in unawaited .forEach() loops at every call site (handleCancelBooking.ts:485, handleNewBooking.ts:966, workflows.tsx:212). Because .forEach() doesn't await async callbacks, deletion failures are silently lost and the caller proceeds without knowing whether reminders were actually cancelled. Consider using Promise.all(reminders.map(...)) at the call sites.": 0.8949967622756958, "The immediateDelete path cancels the email in SendGrid but returns without deleting or marking the workflowReminder DB record as cancelled. This leaves an orphaned row that the cron job won't pick up (it only processes cancelled: true). Add a DB delete or update after the SendGrid cancel request.": 0.9648000001907349, "If twilio.cancelSMS() throws, the prisma.workflowReminder.delete() call is skipped, leaving a stale reminder record that could still trigger an SMS. Wrap each operation in its own try/catch, or move the DB delete into a finally block so the record is always cleaned up.": 0.9330748319625854, "The try/catch wraps the entire loop, so one SendGrid failure aborts cancellation of all remaining reminders and also skips the Promise.all that deletes successfully-cancelled records from the DB. Move error handling inside the loop so each reminder is processed independently.": 0.9871618151664734, "Filter cancellation candidates to scheduled email reminders with a valid referenceId before calling SendGrid cancel; otherwise invalid batch IDs can break cancellation.": 0.9224337339401245, "Use Boolean @default(false) instead of Boolean? for the cancelled field. A nullable boolean creates three states (true/false/null) that complicate queries. The CRON job in scheduleEmailReminders.ts that schedules unscheduled reminders does not filter out cancelled: true records \u2014 so a cancelled reminder whose scheduledDate falls between 1\u201372 hours from now can still be picked up and sent.": 0.9402331709861755, "Unused import: Prisma is imported but no longer referenced anywhere in workflows.tsx file (the Prisma.BatchPayload usage was removed with the deleteReminderPromise array).": 0.3573182225227356}